\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Gaussian expectation is a polynomial state}
\date{2026-10-25}

\p{For positive self-adjoint #{Q} on a finite real inner-product space,
its [expectation](fdip-0006) restricts to a
[real algebraic state](fdip-0024) on the actual
[polynomial function algebra](fdip-002V), with identity involution.}
\proof{
\p{[Absolute polynomial moments](fdip-002W) make the integral defined on
the entire algebra, including every square. Linearity of integration
gives real linearity. The [probability law](fdip-0005) gives
#{\omega_Q(1)=1}. Positivity follows from
##{\omega_Q(P^*P)=\omega_Q(P^2)\geq0.}
Hermiticity is a separate check: since #{P^*=P} and conjugation on
#{\mathbb R} is the identity, #{\omega_Q(P^*)=\omega_Q(P)}.
More generally every pointwise nonnegative polynomial has nonnegative
expectation. In dimension zero this is evaluation at zero on constants.}
}
\p{This is the direct integral realization of the convention in
\citet{Section 3.1, p. 9; Definitions 3.7 and 3.9, Remark 3.10(iv), p. 11}{waldmann2004states},
specialized to ordinary real coefficients as in \ref{fdip-0024}.
A supplied unital star-compatible algebra map permits
[state pullback](fdip-0027), in particular the
[coordinate restriction pullback](fdip-002A). This asserts neither an
automatic Clifford-algebra state nor a conditional expectation.}
